EU ministers of finance will start their  talks with a general discussion on the  economic situation in the European Union  they will also take stock of work on  flexibility under the EU stability and  growth pact and financial assistance to  Romania ministers will also examine  ongoing work on the proposed European  fund for strategic investments which is  one of the core elements of the  Commission's 315 billion euros  investment plan for Europe the aim is to  reach a final agreement by June to  enable cash to start flowing by mid-2015  the fund will support job creating  projects in areas such as transport  energy and broadband infrastructure  education research and innovation  ministers will also discuss in-depth  reviews of the macroeconomic imbalances  in 16 Member States published by the  Commission in March these yearly reviews  aim at helping countries prevent &amp;  correct their macroeconomic imbalances  and to create conditions for sustainable  growth in the European Union the council  will also take a look at the  implementation of its 2014 country  specific recommendations on economic  employment and fiscal policies under the  European semester the e u--'s annual  policy monitoring process finally  ministers will look at the projections  for age-related expenditure in pensions  health care or unemployment benefits in  the 28 member states until 2060 they  will also discuss the results of the  last g20 finance meeting in Washington  in April
 

